  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently listMethods fails (stack trace below) if a CModel object is not found.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It should gracefully handle missing CModel objects (eg specifying a CModel URI simply to identify the type of object without actually wanting to create a CModel object).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This means if an object subscribes to a set of CModels, and any single one of these doesn't exist as a Fedora CModel object it is not possible to list/execute methods for those that do exist.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
